N0017,2016-03-08,politics,Mumbai civic body clears Rs 858 crore budget for roads and drainage,"MUMBAI, Mar 8 — The municipal corporation in Mumbai on Tuesday approved a budget outlay of Rs 858 crore for road repairs and storm-water drainage. Officials said work on 12 priority stretches will begin once tenders are finalised. “Our priority is to ensure that people are not inconvenienced,” said Laura Patel, a police spokesperson.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Metro Ledger
